From 33c0769c5964ecda77bcdbd53aa5f7cb21ada02a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hannes Frederic Sowa <hannes@stressinduktion.org>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2015 22:40:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ipv4: add defensive check for CHECKSUM_PARTIAL skbs in
 ip_fragment
Git-commit: dbd3393c56a8794fe596e7dd20d0efa613b9cf61
Patch-mainline: v4.3-rc7
References: bsc#1285684

CHECKSUM_PARTIAL skbs should never arrive in ip_fragment. If we get one
of those warn about them once and handle them gracefully by recalculating
the checksum.

Cc: Eric Dumazet <edumazet@google.com>
Cc: Vlad Yasevich <vyasevich@gmail.com>
Cc: Benjamin Coddington <bcodding@redhat.com>
Cc: Tom Herbert <tom@herbertland.com>
Signed-off-by: Hannes Frederic Sowa <hannes@stressinduktion.org>
Signed-off-by: David S. Miller <davem@davemloft.net>
Signed-off-by: Ales Novak <alnovak@suse.com>
---
 net/ipv4/ip_output.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/ipv4/ip_output.c b/net/ipv4/ip_output.c
index 9c772aa4f27ff..ce6546afd6e8d 100644
--- a/net/ipv4/ip_output.c
+++ b/net/ipv4/ip_output.c
@@ -464,6 +464,11 @@ int ip_fragment(struct sk_buff *skb, int (*output)(struct sk_buff *))
 
 	dev = rt->dst.dev;
 
+	/* for offloaded checksums cleanup checksum before fragmentation */
+	if (skb->ip_summed == CHECKSUM_PARTIAL &&
+	    (err = skb_checksum_help(skb)))
+		goto fail;
+
 	/*
 	 *	Point into the IP datagram header.
 	 */
-- 
2.56.0

